    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "Minor in Nonprofit and Voluntary Sector Management"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Minors",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Minors",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2026-2027/minors/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "The Minor in Nonprofit and Voluntary Sector Management enables students to focus on the theoretical knowledge and practical competencies required for work in and with the nonprofit sector. The Minor provides the student with an in-depth, interdisciplinary perspective from business and public administration in considering issues critical to this sector."
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Administered by: Faculty of Arts"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "To receive this Minor, students must complete six (6) courses from the following curriculum:"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Required courses (2):"
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "INP 900 Understanding the Nonprofit Sector",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "INP 900",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2026-2027/courses/nonprofit/INP/900/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "INP 901 Developing Effective Organizations",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "INP 901",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2026-2027/courses/nonprofit/INP/901/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Plus four (4) of the following:"
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "INP 912 Marketing for Nonprofit Organizations or MKT 100 Principles of Marketing",
      "links": [
        {
